# UI

Public pages and the signed-in shell use the Costa tokens in `src/app/globals.css` (`--public-*`): fog, ink, secondary text, and accent, with DM Sans. The word Releva uses Instrument Serif italic. Controls inside a signed-in page use the indigo kit in `src/components/ui/form` (`#465ab4`). Read `docs/DESIGN.md` before a visual change. Do not restyle one palette into the other.

Anonymized project cards keep a short metric row (facturación, EBITDA, EBITDA ajustado, precio). Do not build a dense listings table.

- Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only for state, events, or browser APIs.
- Fields, buttons, cards, and tags come from `src/components/ui/form`. Custom dropdowns are `OptionSelect`. Do not use `src/components/ui/button.tsx` on a product screen, and do not add a second menu.
- Style with Tailwind utilities. No CSS-in-JS and no new component library.
- Primitives stay in `src/components/ui`. Feature components stay in `src/components/<feature>` (seller, investor, admin, auth, shell, …).
- Named exports only.
- Every input has a visible label. Interactive controls are buttons or links, not clickable divs.
- Format money in euros from integer cents. Never show a legal company name, CIF, or data-room file on a public page.
- Signed-in layout lives in `src/app/globals.css`: `.shell`, `.layout-page`, `.layout-cards`, and `.layout-table`. Phone is up to 639px, tablet 640–1023, laptop 1024–1279, and desktop from 1280. A new signed-in page uses those classes. Do not add a fixed width, or a four-column grid that stays four columns on a phone or a tablet.

```tsx
// Good: server component, named export, no client boundary
export function ProjectCard({ project }: { project: PublicProject }) {
  return (
    <article>
      <h2>{project.codename}</h2>
      <p>{formatEur(project.revenueCents)}</p>
    </article>
  );
}
```
